{
  "id": "law_of_sines",
  "title": "Law of Sines",
  "description": "Calculate the angles in a generic triangle using the Law of Sines",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Law of Sines\n\nThe \"Law of Sines\" can be used to calculate the angles of a triangle.\n\nThe Law of Sines states that the ratio of the length of a side of a triangle to the sine of the angle opposite that side is constant for all three sides and angles.\n\n**Variables:**\n- a, b, c = length of sides in triangle (m, ft ...)\n- A, B, C = angles in the triangle (degrees)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "side_a",
          "label": "Side a",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "m"
        },
        {
          "id": "side_b",
          "label": "Side b",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 15,
          "unit": "m"
        },
        {
          "id": "side_c",
          "label": "Side c",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 20,
          "unit": "m"
        },
        {
          "id": "angle_A",
          "label": "Angle A",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 30,
          "unit": "degrees"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "angle_B",
          "label": "Angle B",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "ASIN(inputs.side_b * SIN(RADIANS(inputs.angle_A)) / inputs.side_a) * 180 / PI()"
        },
        {
          "id": "angle_C",
          "label": "Angle C",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "180 - inputs.angle_A - ASIN(inputs.side_b * SIN(RADIANS(inputs.angle_A)) / inputs.side_a) * 180 / PI()"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
        "Value",
        "Unit",
        "Description"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Side a",
          "inputs.side_a",
          "m",
          "Length of side a"
        ],
        [
          "Side b",
          "inputs.side_b",
          "m",
          "Length of side b"
        ],
        [
          "Side c",
          "inputs.side_c",
          "m",
          "Length of side c"
        ],
        [
          "Angle A",
          "inputs.angle_A",
          "degrees",
          "Angle A of the triangle"
        ],
        [
          "Angle B",
          "ASIN(inputs.side_b * SIN(RADIANS(inputs.angle_A)) / inputs.side_a) * 180 / PI()",
          "degrees",
          "Calculated angle B"
        ],
        [
          "Angle C",
          "180 - inputs.angle_A - ASIN(inputs.side_b * SIN(RADIANS(inputs.angle_A)) / inputs.side_a) * 180 / PI()",
          "degrees",
          "Calculated angle C"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}